    "name": "maskaravivek"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@mdedit/mcp-server",
  "readme": "# @mdedit/mcp-server\n\nUse mdedit.ai Markdown Documents from ChatGPT, Claude Code, and other Model Context\nProtocol clients. UI-capable MCP Apps hosts receive a rich Markdown reader;\nordinary clients keep the same text and resource-link fallbacks. The server runs locally over stdio and authenticates with a\nscoped API key. It can also reuse an OAuth sign-in created by `mdedit auth login`\nand stored in your operating system keychain, where that sign-in is available.\n\n## Claude Code setup\n\nThe setup available to everyone uses a scoped API key:\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add --transport stdio \\\n  --env MDEDIT_API_KEY=mdh_your_key \\\n  mdedit -- npx -y @mdedit/mcp-server\n```\n\nUse `--scope user` before `mdedit` if you want the server available in every project. Verify the connection with `claude mcp get mdedit` or `/mcp` inside Claude Code.\n\nOAuth sign-in is being rolled out gradually. If it is available for your account,\nrun `mdedit auth login` first and then use the same `claude mcp add` command\nwithout the API-key environment value. Otherwise, use an API key.\n\nReviewer agents normally use `articles:read,reviews:write`. Editing agents need `articles:write`. Accepting a suggestion also requires `articles:write` because it changes document content.\nAgents that publish public links need `publishing:write`; publication status only needs\n`publishing:read`.\n\n## Tools\n\n- `list_workspaces`\n- `list_articles`\n- `create_article`\n- `read_article`\n- `render_article`\n- `start_article_export`\n- `get_article_export_status`\n- `publish_article`\n- `get_publish_status`\n- `unpublish_article`\n- `edit_article`\n- `add_comment`\n- `add_suggestion`\n- `accept_suggestion`\n- `reject_suggestion`\n- `reply_to_thread`\n- `resolve_thread`\n- `list_review_threads`\n- `get_presence`\n\n`publish_article` and `unpublish_article` require explicit confirmation fields in\ntheir tool inputs. A published document is readable by anyone with its `mded.it` link.\n\nWhen `mode` is omitted, `publish_article` asks the API to use Live only if it creates\nthe first link; an existing link keeps its stored mode. Pass `mode: \"snapshot\"` or\n`mode: \"live\"` to choose or switch deliberately. This is one atomic publish request,\nso agents do not need a status preflight before publishing.\n\n`publish_article` and `get_publish_status` return the stored mode, source\nrevision/version, last successful sync time, and synchronization status. A failed Live\nsync leaves the last good public content and URL available; inspect `syncStatus` and\n`syncError` before claiming the public page is current.\n\nLocal stdio keeps one live collaborative session open across tool calls. The\nhosted HTTP adapter uses operation-scoped sessions and does not depend on\nprocess-local state or load-balancer stickiness. Non-collaborative documents use\nthe REST fallback and report an empty live-presence list.\n\n`render_article` owns the versioned `ui://mdedit/article/v5` MCP App resource. The URI changes when the bundled UI changes so clients do not reuse a stale cached app, while editor links returned by the server use the canonical `https://app.mdedit.ai/doc/:id` route.\nIts model-visible result is deliberately concise; full Markdown, routing data,\npermissions, review state, publication state, and signed media mappings are\ncomponent-only metadata. Raw author HTML is disabled. GitHub Gists are fetched as\nbounded code, YouTube and Vimeo are click-to-load, and passive remote media uses\nshort-lived mdedit proxy URLs.\n\n## Environment\n\n- `MDEDIT_API_KEY` - optional scoped API key override; takes precedence over OAuth\n- `MDEDIT_PROFILE` - optional shared OAuth profile name; defaults to the active CLI profile\n- `MDEDIT_API_URL` \u2014 optional API host override\n- `MDEDIT_AGENT_NAME` \u2014 optional awareness display hint; defaults to `mdedit-mcp`\n- `MDEDIT_MCP_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` \u2014 optional positive idle timeout in milliseconds\n\nNever commit API keys to a repository or place them in shared project MCP configuration.\n\n## Maintainer launch gate\n\nThe repository includes a manual Claude Code smoke test. It creates a uniquely named fixture article in the selected test workspace, enables collaboration, exercises list/read/comment/list/resolve/presence through MCP, verifies the resolved comment through the review API, and deletes the fixture.\n\n```bash\nMDEDIT_API_KEY=mdh_launch_gate_key \\\nMDEDIT_SMOKE_WORKSPACE_ID=workspace_id \\\nyarn workspace @mdedit/mcp-server smoke:claude\n```\n\nUse a test workspace and a key with `articles:write,reviews:write`. The key owner must have access to the workspace and the collaboration entitlement.\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
